WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.200
A swordfish approaches a school of fish, beating its crescent tail.

00:03.200 --> 00:05.200
The bill sweeps sideways. This can stun or injure prey.

00:05.200 --> 00:09.200
The school scatters. The swordfish turns back toward one slowed fish.

00:09.200 --> 00:11.100
The mouth takes in the slowed fish; the bill does not swallow it.

00:11.100 --> 00:14.000
The swordfish swims on. This is an illustrated reconstruction with illustrative timing.
